Lexifina's own contributions to this repository (the arrangement of the history, the file layout, the commit
messages, the tables and the tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

The legal text keeps its sources' own terms:

1. constitution/: the Constitution of Saint Lucia as published in the Revised Laws of Saint Lucia (2023) by the
   Attorney General's Chambers of Saint Lucia (https://www.attorneygeneralchambers.com). The site states no
   licence; its pages say "All Rights Reserved".

2. acts/ and statutory-instruments/: Acts of Parliament and Statutory Instruments as printed by the National
   Printing Corporation, the Government Printer of Saint Lucia (https://npc.govt.lc/laws/acts,
   https://npc.govt.lc/laws/si). The site states no licence or terms of use for these files.

Under the Copyright Act of Saint Lucia (Cap. 13.07), section 24(4) and (5), copyright in works made or first
published by or under the direction of the Government belongs initially to the Crown. The text is reproduced
without change to its wording, as a public record of the law, with attribution to its publishers.

Changes made by Lexifina: the text was converted to one Markdown file per provision; running heads and page
numbers were removed from the PDF text layers, and the amendment notes printed under each provision of the
Revised Laws were left out. Lexifina does not claim that either publisher endorses this repository.
